      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine the volume of each cube. The volume \\(V\\) of a cube with edge length \\(s\\) is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ V = s^3 \\]\n\nFirst, let's find the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches. Since 1 foot is equal to 12 inches, the edge length of 1 foot is equal to 12 inches. Therefore, the volume \\(V_1\\) of the cube with edge length 12 inches is:\n\n\\[ V_1 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches. Let's calculate this:\n\n\\[ V_2 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nNow we can compute the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube. It will be:\n\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{1728}{216} \\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1728 and 216. Let's use Python to find the GCD and simplify the fraction.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Volumes\nV1 = 12**3\nV2 = 6**3\n\n# Ratio\nratio = V1 / V2\n\n# Simplifying the fraction\ngcd = math.gcd(V1, V2)\nsimplified_ratio = (V1 // gcd, V2 // gcd)\n\nprint((ratio, simplified_ratio))\n```\n```output\n(8.0, (216, 1))\n```\nThe ratio of the volume of a cube with edge length six inches to the volume of a cube with edge length one foot is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = 8 \\]\n\nSo, in fractional form:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{8}{1}} \\]\n\nThis simplifies to 8.",
