      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine the volume of each cube. The volume \\(V\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula \\(V = s^3\\).\n\nFor the cube with an edge length of six inches:\n\\[\nV_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\nFor the cube with an edge length of one foot (which is 12 inches):\n\\[\nV_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube. The ratio is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. \n\nThe prime factorizations are:\n\\[\n216 = 2^3 \\times 3^3\n\\]\n\\[\n1728 = 2^6 \\times 3^3\n\\]\n\nThe common factors are \\(2^3\\) and\\(3^3\\), so the GCD is:\n\\[\n2^3 \\times 3^3 = 8 \\times 27 = 216\n\\]\n\nWe divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD, which is 216:\n\\[\n\\frac{216}{1728} = \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the volume of a cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of a cube with an edge length of one foot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\n\\]",
