      "text": "To find the ratio of the volume of a cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of a cube with an edge length of one foot, we need to first convert the edge lengths from inches to feet. There are 12 inches in a foot, so a cube with an edge length of one foot is actually 1 inch*12/36 inch ≈ 0.29 feet.\n\nThe volume of a cube is calculated by raising the side length to the third power. Therefore, we calculate:\n\nVolume of the first cube (with edge length 6 inches) = 6^3 = 216\n\nVolume of the second cube (with edge length 1 inch*12/36) = (12/36)^3 = (1/3)^3 = 1/27\n\nNow we need to find the ratio of the two volumes:\n\nRatio = 216 / (1/27) = 216 * 27 = 5832\n\nThe ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot should be expressed as a common fraction, which means we need to find the simplified form of the fraction 5832/1.\n\nWe can use prime factorization to simplify the fraction:\n\n- 5832 can be written as 2^4 * 3^4 * 11\n- We know that 11 = 11\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of 5832/1 is:\n\n5832/1 = (2^4 * 3^4 * 11) / 1 = 2^4 * 3^4 * 11\n\nSo the final answer is: \\boxed{\\frac{26244}{1}}",
